ommit_sha":"afb2b315f798a0dd3e4a5fa259367d47c7a746e9","position":"1786766840150783001-6261b453-3a7f-4d7a-84b0-7ba266e602a3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786763238956278001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe READ-ONLY, S3-backed live **Jira Cloud** multi-project bridge rehearsal was\ndropped when the effort pivoted to Jira Data Center. Sibling story 368f landed the\nDC harness (git/file-backed, throwaway low-volume projects). Two dimensions DC\ncannot exercise remain uncovered: the **S3 store backend** and **real Cloud ticket\nvolume/diversity** across the two real Cloud projects **REB** and **DIG**. This\nstory restores that coverage — strictly read-only against Cloud.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a new opt-in live suite `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/` that drives the\nreconciler against REB + DIG over an ISOLATED, S3-backed copy of the ticket store,\nusing ONLY read paths proven non-mutating on Jira:\n- **Inbound fetch** via `rebar_reconciler.fetcher.compute_snapshot(...)` — the\n  read-only counterpart of `fetch_snapshot` (writes nothing; only issues JQL\n  searches). The store's `projects.json` mapping drives a per-project JQL fan-out\n  (`fetcher._build_snapshot`), so a REB+DIG mapping fetches both projects.\n- **`rebar.bridge_preview(...)`** — dry-run (`Mode.DRY_RUN` → `MODE_CAPS=0` →\n  `persist=False`), so no leaf applier runs and nothing is written to Jira or the\n  store.\nStructural read-only enforcement: an autouse fixture monkeypatches every mutating\nmethod on the Cloud transport class (`AcliClient.create_issue/update_issue/\nadd_comment/add_label/remove_label/set_entity_property/delete_issue/\ntransition_issue_by_name/unassign_issue/set_parent/update_priority/\nupdate_issuetype/update_comment/delete_comment/delete_issue_link`) to raise, so the\nsuite is STRUCTURALLY unable to invoke an outbound Jira mutation; read methods are\nuntouched. Every Jira-touching scenario also asserts per-project issue counts are\nidentical before and after (belt-and-braces).\nThe store is a FRESH, isolated store (never the production remote): its ONLY git\nremote is a throwaway `s3://<bucket>/<unique-prefix>` wired via `git-remote-s3`,\nwith `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off`. Store CONTENT is irrelevant to a read-only fetch (volume\ncomes from live Jira), so a minimal store is the correct, lighter isolation\nboundary — it cannot reach production. The prefix is deleted in teardown.\nAvoiding the prior failure: map ONLY real, reachable projects (REB, DIG). One\nnegative-control scenario maps an UNKNOWN key and asserts the fetch FAILS CLOSED\n(raises), never silently succeeds — the documented correct behaviour.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/conftest.py` (new) — gating sentinel\n  `_live_jira_ready` (earns `jira_live`), the isolated S3 store fixture, the\n  structural read-only guard fixture, and the throwaway-prefix teardown.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` (new) — the\n  read-only scenarios below.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/README.md` (new) — runbook + env vars.\n- `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` (edit) — a new manually-dispatched\n  `jira-cloud-s3-rehearsal` job running `pytest -m external\n  tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3 -q -rA`, plus `--ignore=tests/external/\n  live_jira_cloud_s3` on the existing `external` job so it is not double-collected.\nThis is a test/CI-only change; no `src/rebar` runtime code changes.\n\n## Testing\nThis ticket IS a live test suite. Scenarios (all read-only):\n1. `test_one_store_maps_both_projects` — the S3 store maps REB and DIG with the\n   expected repo lists; its only remote is the throwaway S3 prefix.\n2. `test_inbound_fetch_pulls_both_projects` — `compute_snapshot` with REB+DIG mapped\n   yields keys from BOTH projects at real volume (each project > 0; total in the\n   thousands), every key ∈ {REB,DIG} (per-project attribution via key prefix).\n3. `test_fetch_is_scoped_per_project` — REB-only mapping → snapshot ⊆ REB and zero\n   DIG; DIG-only → ⊆ DIG and zero REB (mapping scopes the fetch; no contamination).\n4. `test_bridge_preview_read_only_and_scoped` — `bridge_preview` plan targets only\n   REB/DIG; per-project Jira counts identical before/after.\n5. `test_s3_store_roundtrips_with_mapping_intact` — push the store's `tickets`\n   branch to the S3 prefix, clone it back, assert the REB+DIG mapping survives.\n6. `test_unknown_project_fails_closed` — an unknown mapped key makes `compute_snapshot`\n   RAISE (fail-closed), never a silent empty fetch.\n7. `test_read_only_guard_is_real` — calling a patched mutator raises, proving the\n   structural guard is not vacuous.\nLocal validation: `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy` on the new files;\n`pytest --collect-only`; then a real green `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1 pytest -m external\ntests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3 -q -rA` against live REB+DIG+S3.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The new suite exists under `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/`, is gated by\n      `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL` + Jira/AWS creds, and enforces the read-only invariant\n      STRUCTURALLY (verified: `test_read_only_guard_is_real` passes and the guard\n      fixture is autouse on every Jira-touching test).\n- [ ] It is wired into CI as a dedicated `jira-cloud-s3-rehearsal` job in\n      `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`, and the `external` job ignores\n      the new dir (verified by reading the workflow).\n- [ ] An ACTUAL green live run demonstrates all five validations — both projects\n      fetched into one S3 store, correct per-project resolution, read-only preview\n      scoping, S3 round-trip, and ZERO Jira writes (verified: the captured\n      `-rA` run output is attached as a ticket comment, showing before/after Jira\n      counts equal and the guard active).\n- [ ] The throwaway S3 prefix is deleted after the run (verified: an `aws s3 ls`\n      of the prefix returns empty, recorded on the ticket).\n- [ ] `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, and `mypy` pass on the new files.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/conftest.py","reason":"new: gating sentinel, isolated S3 store fixture, structural read-only guard, throwaway-prefix teardown"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py","reason":"new: read-only REB+DIG over-S3 scenarios (fetch spread, per-project scoping, preview read-only, S3 round-trip, fail-closed, guard)"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/README.md","reason":"new: runbook and env-var reference for the read-only Cloud+S3 rehearsal"},{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"edit: add jira-cloud-s3-rehearsal job; ignore the new dir in the external job to avoid double-collection"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"e14e09e5-8dba-4af3-8f0e-23ea4ad136cc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5014-d0c6-5bbe-47fb","ticket_type":"story","title":"Read-only S3-backed live Jira Cloud multi-project rehearsal (REB + DIG)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d71a6c61-8c03-4e0e-b1e8-01d4066d571b","445ede28-d061-4c7c-929e-3f8848f9b71b","7e4a88c8-e9e2-45e7-a5f8-25a0bde7321b","dbc0b480-2503-442d-b9be-fe32b02f3c74","e14e09e5-8dba-4af3-8f0e-23ea4ad136cc","6261b453-3a7f-4d7a-84b0-7ba266e602a3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786772514005706001,"uuid":"be6f71f4-96c6-4d49-bdd6-6815a7de441f"}